<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36202" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντέμνω</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντεμεν-τάμνω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cut in, engrave upon,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τοῖσι λίθοισι γράμματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.22
				</span></i>
			; of a map, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χάλκεον πίνακα, ἐν τῷ γῆς . .
					περίοδος ἐνετέτμητο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					5.49
				</span></i>
			: <i>cut</i> or <i>scoop</i> a hollow in a thing, in 
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντετμέαται</span> Hp <i><span class="en">
				<u>Art.</u>
				72
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντετμημένου τοῦ σπληνίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orib.
					46.25.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>cut up a victim, sacrifice,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἥρωϊ</span> to a hero, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				5.11
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Scyth.</u>
				1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. σφάγιά τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Sol.</u>
					9
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ . . ἵππον τόμιον
				ἐντεμοίμεθα</span>
			<i>should get</i> it <i>cut up,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				192
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐντέμνεται σφάγια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dion.Byz.
					14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>cut in, shred in,</i> of herbs in a remedy, metaph., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>cut,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ναῦς ἐ. κύματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.352
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				22
			</span></i> (
				Pass.
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tox.</u>
				37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tox.</u>
				37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hist.Conscr.</u>
				25
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
